<%# The feed's pagination control. `data-turbo-stream` makes Turbo request
    `index.turbo_stream.erb`, which appends the next page and replaces this row.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.3) — deliberately NOT `ds_button_classes`. The
    design system's Button is a pill, and its one non-pill variant (`link`) is the bare
    text control inside a notification row: `border-0 bg-transparent p-0 inline-flex`.
    This is a full-width centred row with its own `py-3` tap target, so asking for that
    variant would mean overriding display AND padding — same-family utilities, which
    resolve by their order in the bundle rather than the caller's (see the `padded:`
    note in ui/_card). It is already the DS's link treatment otherwise: primary indigo,
    medium weight. Left alone on purpose. %>
<%= link_to "Load more",
      root_path(page: @pagy.next, filter: params[:filter]),
      data: { turbo_stream: true },
      class: "block text-center text-primary font-medium py-3" %>
